<title>USA: General Bearing Corp Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>General Bearing Corp Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>WEST NYACK, N.Y. 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share figures)</p>
<p>					    First Quarter Ended,</p>
<p>					   3/29/97	 3/30/96</p>
<p> Sales				    $9,592	  $9,918</p>
<p> Cost of sales			   6,735	   7,460</p>
<p>    Gross profit			 2,857	   2,458</p>
<p> SG&amp;A					2,098	   1,827</p>
<p> Operating Income			  759	     631</p>
<p>Other Expense:  Interest, net,</p>
<p>including $5,714 &amp; $37,500</p>
<p>  to parent				  281	     331</p>
<p>Income before income tax</p>
<p>  benefit &amp; extraordinary income     478	     300</p>
<p> Income tax (benefit)		  (389)	     114</p>
<p> Net Income				  867	     186</p>
<p> Income Per Share			 0.25	    0.06</p>
<p>Weighted Average</p>
<p>  Shares Outstanding	     3,494,500     3,000,000</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said Q1 1997 includes a gain of $389,000 compared to a tax provision loss of $114,000 in 1996 related to its anticipated use of net operating loss carry-forwards.</p>
</text>
